95 0 obj
<</A 261 0 R /Alt
  (Figure 4 shows the average change in sentiment model scores when substituting each individual phrase \(as opposed to grouped by disability categories shown in Figure 1\). The term "a person who walks with a limp" results in the highest negative sentiment \association --- it shifts the score to more negative by almost -0.25\(in a -1 to +1 scale\).\n␀)
  /ID (AD000000-0000-0000-ADBE-       14914) /K 2 /P 78 0 R /Pg 185 0 R
  /S /Figure>>
