  (Figure 5 shows words produced by BERT in the fill-in-the-blank analysis for sentences containing disability terms that produced negative sentiment scores. The words ranged from relatively less negative words like injured and invisible to highly negative w\ords such as rejected, banned, abnormal etc. The most common negative word that BERT produced was punished, which occurred almost 29% of the cases.␀)
