2433 0 obj
<</A 2438 0 R /Alt
  (Figure 1 shows the average change in the model score when substituting pronouns with disability mentions in sentences in our corpus. Recommended and non-recommended phrases are grouped separately, denoted in blue vs. yellow. The figure shows the results f\or both toxicity model \(on left\) and sentiment model \(on right\). Across board, for both models, non-recommended phrases resulted in a higher shift in scores \(i.e., more toxic, or more negative sentiment\) than recommended phrases --- which is as expe\cted. However, many recommended phrases are also associated with toxicity/negativity which might result in innocuous sentences discussing disability being penalized. ␀)
  /ID (AD000000-0000-0000-ADBE-       13402) /K 0 /P 10 0 R /Pg 704 0 R
  /S /Figure>>
endobj
